    {
      "id": "06af02f3-829c-4114-8733-1e2a4c53b959",
      "userId": "test",
      "title": "What is contract law?",
      "messages": [
        {
          "role": "user",
          "content": "What is contract law?",
          "timestamp": "2026-04-10T06:29:07.452Z",
          "attachments": []
        },
        {
          "role": "ai",
          "content": "Contract law is the body of law that governs agreements between people or organizations. It determines when an agreement is legally enforceable and what happens if one side does not do what they promised.\n\nIn general, contract law covers:\n- **Offer and acceptance**: one party makes an offer, and the other agrees to it.\n- **Consideration**: each side gives something of value.\n- **Intention to create legal relations**: the parties meant the agreement to be legally binding.\n- **Capacity and legality**: the parties must be able to contract, and the purpose must be lawful.\n\nIf a valid contract is broken, the law may provide remedies such as:\n- **Damages**: money compensation\n- **Specific performance**: a court order to carry out the promise\n- **Cancellation or rescission**: ending the contract\n\nContract law is important in everyday life, from buying goods and signing leases to employment and business deals.",
          "timestamp": "2026-04-10T06:29:12.103Z",
          "attachments": []
        }
      ],
      "createdAt": "2026-04-10T06:29:07.452Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-04-10T06:29:12.103Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "d2ae9473-42b7-4ce1-8f2d-576e41fb3e4a",
      "userId": "359adb86-14d0-46a2-9588-2141101999cf",
      "title": "Qul olish qonuniymi?>",
      "messages": [
        {
